{"type":"standard","title":"Kat Cammack","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kat Cammack</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q98523243","titles":{"canonical":"Kat_Cammack","normalized":"Kat Cammack","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kat Cammack</span></span>"},"pageid":64630182,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Rep._Kat_Cammack_official_photo%2C_117th_Congress_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg/330px-Rep._Kat_Cammack_official_photo%2C_117th_Congress_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":438},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Rep._Kat_Cammack_official_photo%2C_117th_Congress_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":917,"height":1216},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1361106042","tid":"71c39081-70bc-11f1-b90a-388d9e1ed516","timestamp":"2026-06-25T17:36:49Z","description":"American politician (born 1988)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kat_Cammack","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kat_Cammack?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kat_Cammack?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kat_Cammack"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kat_Cammack","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Kat_Cammack","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kat_Cammack?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kat_Cammack"}},"extract":"Kathryn Christine Cammack is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 3rd congressional district. A member of the Republican Party, Cammack previously served as deputy chief of staff to her predecessor, Representative Ted Yoho, who retired in 2020. Her congressional district covers a twelve-county area that includes much of North Central Florida.","extract_html":"<p><b>Kathryn Christine Cammack</b> is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 3rd congressional district. A member of the Republican Party, Cammack previously served as deputy chief of staff to her predecessor, Representative Ted Yoho, who retired in 2020. Her congressional district covers a twelve-county area that includes much of North Central Florida.</p>"}